WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.059
This is one page of an e-bike manual.

2
00:00:03.059 --> 00:00:05.263
Now, watch the same steps.

3
00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.940
Remove the fork spacer, and pull the pad spacer out of the

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.147
caliper. Do not squeeze the brake lever.

5
00:00:12.797 --> 00:00:15.235
The fork arch faces forward.

6
00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:17.042
Bring the wheel up between the legs,

7
00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:19.337
with the rotor on the caliper side.

8
00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:22.591
Guide the rotor into the caliper slot,

9
00:00:22.591 --> 00:00:25.286
exactly between the two brake pads.

10
00:00:26.387 --> 00:00:29.882
Push the wheel up, until both ends of the hub sit fully in the

11
00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:31.058
dropouts.

12
00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:35.696
Push the skewer through, with a spring on each side,

13
00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.217
small end inward.

14
00:00:37.217 --> 00:00:40.655
Hold the lever open, and tighten the nut until it is snug.

15
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:42.713
Now close the lever.

16
00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:45.359
You must feel resistance from halfway.

17
00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:47.763
Never spin it like a wing nut.

18
00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:49.960
Spin the wheel.

19
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.212
If the rotor rubs, loosen the two caliper bolts,

20
00:00:53.212 --> 00:00:54.826
squeeze and hold the brake lever,

21
00:00:54.826 --> 00:00:56.231
then tighten the bolts.

22
00:00:57.931 --> 00:01:01.973
A straight wheel, a quiet brake, and a safe first ride.
